First Day in London — rubber-hose style test (17 s)

Picture: made entirely in code (Canvas 2D). Rendering engine pieces (toon.js line engine,
film.js gate/damage pass, parts.js pie eyes / gloves / shoes / hose limbs) adapted from the
lemo-opuscar library's rubber-hose style demo (technique reuse; no story, shots or characters reused).

Voice: test_audio.wav, supplied by the production (unchanged).

Fonts (all SIL Open Font License 1.1, Google Fonts, self-hosted in fonts/):
- IM Fell English SC — Igino Marini (dialogue cards)              fonts/OFL-imfellenglishsc.txt
- Limelight — Eben Sorkin (sign lettering, speaker tabs)          fonts/OFL-limelight.txt
- Shrikhand — Jonny Pinhorn (loaded, title face for the series)    fonts/OFL-shrikhand.txt
- Aref Ruqaa — Abdullah Aref, Khaled Hosny (Arabic narration)      fonts/OFL-arefruqaa.txt
- Fredoka, Lilita One, Baloo Bhaijaan 2, Lalezar (series fonts, Arabic fallback) — OFL, copied from a1-u1-l01/fonts

Mastering: ffmpeg two-pass loudnorm (-14 LUFS) + film grain, via mux_local.sh (copy of the library's mux.sh
with the false "only 14 s decodable" length check relaxed to a warning).
